%% ======================================================================================
%% CONCIERGE FSM — LATEST ARCHITECTURE (2026-06-25)
%% ======================================================================================
%% Source: k1/concierge/fsm/*.py (16 files, ~9,876 lines)
%% Branch: feature/prompt-architecture-refactor
%% The FSM is the event router. It does NOT drive a loop.
%% It subscribes to 27+ bus topics, routes events, manages
%% concurrency between Front and Back, and controls all state
%% transitions. It is the SINGLE WRITER to SessionState
%% (via TaskBridge + HistoryWriter + ControlExtension).
%% ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLES:
%%   1. Event-driven: FSM subscribes to bus, transitions on events
%%   2. Guard-first: Every (state, topic) has a guard action
%%   3. Pure decision tables: response_final_table, arbiter — zero side effects
%%   4. Single Writer: FSM alone writes SS.task_state, SS.task_artifacts, SS.history_active
%%   5. FrontLock serializes Front: no two Front LLM calls concurrently

flowchart TB

